# defconfigs/embedded.config — RISC-V 64 / Generic board / Embedded profile
#
# Target: Generic rv64 microcontroller / minimal SoC with < 2 MiB RAM.
#         Pure profile preset — smallest reasonable configuration on rv64.
#         Use as a starting point for board bring-up on any rv64 platform
#         not yet listed in Kconfig.platform.
#
# Memory budget (rough):
#   Static tables (RFC-0023 embedded): ~50-100 KiB
#   Kernel heap (KERNEL_HEAP_SIZE = 512 KiB, embedded Kconfig default): 512 KiB
#   Task stacks (MAX_TASKS=32 × 16 KiB, demand-paged on rv64 with MMU): ~512 KiB
#   Total worst-case: ~1.1-1.2 MiB  (fits in any target with >= 2 MiB RAM)
#
# Notable vs. edge defaults:
#   ARCH=RISCV64, BOARD=GENERIC (fill in UART_BASE / PLIC_BASE / RAM_BASE manually).
#   PROFILE_EMBEDDED — smallest cap tier (MAX_TASKS=32, TCP_MAX_CONNS=4,
#     KERNEL_HEAP=512 KiB, MAX_CAPS_TOTAL=256, etc.).
#   SCHED_HZ=100 (PROFILE_EMBEDDED default).
#   All drivers still enabled by default — disable per-board as needed.
#   WCET_BOUND_TIMER_ISR_US=10 (real hardware, non-QEMU default).
#   DRV_VIRTIO_BLK_NET=n (auto from !BOARD_QEMU).
#
# Used for: generic rv64 bring-up, minimal kernel validation, platform porting.
#
# Regenerate with:  make defconfig-embedded && make savedefconfig
CONFIG_BOARD_GENERIC=y
CONFIG_PROFILE_EMBEDDED=y
